1
00:00:25,488 --> 00:00:27,917
(Fall is in full swing,)

2
00:00:27,918 --> 00:00:30,058
(surrounded by colorful foliage.)

3
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:32,898
(Today's spare time, Suji, Yongin)

4
00:00:33,428 --> 00:00:36,028
This kind of sunlight is relaxing.

5
00:00:36,428 --> 00:00:38,967
- It's so warm here.
- Right.

6
00:00:38,968 --> 00:00:40,067
(The two of them are sitting in a cafe.)

7
00:00:40,068 --> 00:00:42,337
- Gosh.
- Is it nice and hot?

8
00:00:42,338 --> 00:00:44,708
My gosh. It's warm.

9
00:00:45,338 --> 00:00:47,777
- We're in Yongin, right?
- We're in Suji.

10
00:00:47,778 --> 00:00:49,177
- Suji, Yongin.
- Suji.

11
00:00:49,178 --> 00:00:52,848
Hold on. Suji is a new town.

12
00:00:53,278 --> 00:00:54,478
It's either-or.

13
00:00:55,148 --> 00:00:58,218
Since we're in Suji, the Whenever Friend could be young.

14
00:00:58,518 --> 00:01:01,988
Or it could be someone who enjoys a quieter, rural lifestyle.

15
00:01:02,188 --> 00:01:03,957
- There are a lot of townhouses.
- Right.

16
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:06,127
- There are many townhouses in Suji.
- I see.

17
00:01:06,128 --> 00:01:07,857
- Right. The country lifestyle...
- People with that lifestyle...

18
00:01:07,858 --> 00:01:09,968
- live here too.
- Yes.

19
00:01:10,128 --> 00:01:11,898
The view here is amazing.

20
00:01:12,298 --> 00:01:14,668
They'll stop by the restroom. They're nervous.

21
00:01:15,308 --> 00:01:17,137
- They're stopping by the restroom.
- They're nervous?

22
00:01:17,138 --> 00:01:18,367
- I think...
- Late 30s or early 40s.

23
00:01:18,368 --> 00:01:19,608
They're in their late 30s or early 40s.

24
00:01:20,678 --> 00:01:22,907
They're using the restroom before the shoot.

25
00:01:22,908 --> 00:01:24,708
- Late 30s or early 40s.
- Late 30s or early 40s for sure.

26
00:01:25,048 --> 00:01:26,478
- They must be older than that.
- Yes.

27
00:01:27,018 --> 00:01:28,148
- Right?
- Yes.

28
00:01:28,518 --> 00:01:30,388
- Young people wouldn't need to.
- Right.

29
00:01:30,688 --> 00:01:32,188
- They must be in their 40s.
- Yes.

30
00:01:33,018 --> 00:01:36,158
Oh, look. They're filming something here.

31
00:01:37,088 --> 00:01:38,497
Do you want some coffee?

32
00:01:38,498 --> 00:01:39,527
Sounds good.

33
00:01:39,528 --> 00:01:40,957
(His old-school wit reinforces their reasoning.)

34
00:01:40,958 --> 00:01:42,427
- This place...
- Yes.

35
00:01:42,428 --> 00:01:45,168
used to be a field when I was growing up.

36
00:01:45,538 --> 00:01:46,938
- We were right. He's in his 40s.
- We were right.

37
00:01:47,568 --> 00:01:49,167
(Spotting people in their 30s and 40s)

38
00:01:49,168 --> 00:01:50,908
We were spot on.

39
00:01:51,708 --> 00:01:53,477
- We were spot on.
- Hello.

40
00:01:53,478 --> 00:01:54,878
- Hey, Go Soo.
- Hello.

41
00:01:56,108 --> 00:01:57,947
(Setting the bar high...)

42
00:01:57,948 --> 00:01:59,778
(for good-looking celebrities with his chiseled features)

43
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:02,248
(The original sculpted beauty, Go Soo)

44
00:02:02,988 --> 00:02:05,788
(Exuding charisma with a chic vibe)

45
00:02:06,018 --> 00:02:07,958
(Handsome Man on the Rise, Yuk Seong Jae)

46
00:02:08,188 --> 00:02:10,388
(These two good-looking men worked together on a project.)

47
00:02:10,528 --> 00:02:12,357
Did you know your eyes are sparkling like crazy?

48
00:02:12,358 --> 00:02:13,628
(The heartwarming intern)

49
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:14,797
I'll give you a ride.

50
00:02:14,798 --> 00:02:16,428
(The rational director)

51
00:02:17,298 --> 00:02:19,397
(They're back with a heart-fluttering office romance,)

52
00:02:19,398 --> 00:02:23,108
("Nine to Six.")

53
00:02:23,208 --> 00:02:24,408
Hey, Yeon Seok.

54
00:02:24,708 --> 00:02:25,938
Nice to see you.

55
00:02:26,108 --> 00:02:27,237
Have you been well?

56
00:02:27,238 --> 00:02:28,547
- I've been well.
- I see.

57
00:02:28,548 --> 00:02:30,147
- Have you been well?
- Of course.

58
00:02:30,148 --> 00:02:31,148
Come on in, Seong Jae.

59
00:02:31,278 --> 00:02:33,518
- Let's sit down and talk.
- Hello. Okay.

60
00:02:33,548 --> 00:02:36,348
- The staff doesn't tell us...
- Okay.

61
00:02:36,818 --> 00:02:40,187
who's joining us until they show up.

62
00:02:40,188 --> 00:02:41,188
I see.

63
00:02:41,189 --> 00:02:44,428
We narrowed down the age groups first.

64
00:02:44,828 --> 00:02:47,398
They said you went to the restroom right before the shot.

65
00:02:47,758 --> 00:02:49,128
So I said you had to be in your late 30s or early 40s.

66
00:02:50,228 --> 00:02:52,467
- We said you had to be in your 40s.
- You had to be in your 40s.

67
00:02:52,468 --> 00:02:55,208
Then we said you guys probably had some experience being on TV.

68
00:02:55,638 --> 00:02:57,638
- Over 20 years.
- We knew you had to be experienced.

69
00:02:57,738 --> 00:02:59,307
- Like a TV expert?
- That's right.

70
00:02:59,308 --> 00:03:01,708
That's how you figured out it was Soo.

71
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:04,578
Right. When I saw you guys...

72
00:03:04,678 --> 00:03:07,417
This used to be my old neighborhood.

73
00:03:07,418 --> 00:03:08,517
- I see.
- Okay.

74
00:03:08,518 --> 00:03:10,847
I lived in the apartment nearby. You can see it from here.

75
00:03:10,848 --> 00:03:12,018
- Really?
- Yes.

76
00:03:12,118 --> 00:03:13,687
- Then...
- We're in your hometown.

77
00:03:13,688 --> 00:03:15,587
- I grew up in Suji.
- I came here from time to time.

78
00:03:15,588 --> 00:03:16,588
Can I eat some?

79
00:03:16,589 --> 00:03:17,888
- Go ahead.
- Yes.

80
00:03:17,928 --> 00:03:19,427
- Yes. Try some egg tarts.
- Dig in.

81
00:03:19,428 --> 00:03:20,828
- Go ahead.
- What do you like?

82
00:03:21,628 --> 00:03:23,598
Did you guys film a drama together?

83
00:03:24,068 --> 00:03:27,538
Yes. It's called "Nine to Six." It will premiere on November 25.

84
00:03:27,668 --> 00:03:29,238
- November 25?
- Yes.

85
00:03:29,508 --> 00:03:30,637
As you can tell from the title,

86
00:03:30,638 --> 00:03:33,738
it's a drama about an office romance.

87
00:03:33,908 --> 00:03:35,878
Soo plays...

88
00:03:36,208 --> 00:03:38,007
a rational character.

89
00:03:38,008 --> 00:03:40,948
And his character's future is pretty much set.

90
00:03:41,278 --> 00:03:42,588
But I play an intern.

91
00:03:42,718 --> 00:03:46,457
So financially, my character isn't that ideal.

92
00:03:46,458 --> 00:03:48,258
He's not the best guy realistically.

93
00:03:48,518 --> 00:03:50,057
So because of our difference...

94
00:03:50,058 --> 00:03:51,357
- Is that the conflict?
- That's right.

95
00:03:51,358 --> 00:03:54,358
The drama is about realistic dating dilemmas?

96
00:03:54,428 --> 00:03:56,127
Park Min Young is also in the drama.

97
00:03:56,128 --> 00:03:57,497
- Min Young?
- Yes.

98
00:03:57,498 --> 00:03:58,698
Are you three in a love triangle?

99
00:03:58,798 --> 00:03:59,798
That's right.

100
00:03:59,799 --> 00:04:00,838
(Looking around)

101
00:04:01,138 --> 00:04:02,608
Gosh, it's very hot in here.

102
00:04:03,568 --> 00:04:05,937
Well, Soo...

103
00:04:05,938 --> 00:04:08,107
suffered with the heat the whole time we filmed together.

104
00:04:08,108 --> 00:04:09,708
- Really?
- We...

105
00:04:09,748 --> 00:04:11,278
Actually, I also thought it was getting hot.

106
00:04:11,878 --> 00:04:12,947
- Where are you going?
- Where...

107
00:04:12,948 --> 00:04:14,777
- Sit here. It's shaded here.
- No.

108
00:04:14,778 --> 00:04:17,017
- You should switch places.
- Please turn on the AC.

109
00:04:17,018 --> 00:04:18,247
- Please take my seat.
- Come here.

110
00:04:18,248 --> 00:04:19,458
Please turn on the AC.

111
00:04:19,658 --> 00:04:20,857
- Sit next to me, Soo.
- I was startled.

112
00:04:20,858 --> 00:04:21,927
I thought...

113
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:22,988
- you were going to punch me.
- Here...

114
00:04:24,288 --> 00:04:25,827
- Soo.
- He never disappoints.

115
00:04:25,828 --> 00:04:27,497
We haven't met in a while. I thought you were going to hit me.

116
00:04:27,498 --> 00:04:28,627
It's not that.

117
00:04:28,628 --> 00:04:30,497
- My back was getting really hot.
- Actually, I also...

118
00:04:30,498 --> 00:04:32,367
- The sunlight is really strong.
- It's not that hot outside.

119
00:04:32,368 --> 00:04:35,438
There's no sunlight right up to your spot.

120
00:04:35,468 --> 00:04:38,138
- But your spot...
- My spot got all the sunlight.

121
00:04:38,708 --> 00:04:40,107
(He safely escapes.)

122
00:04:40,108 --> 00:04:42,578
How do you two know each other?

123
00:04:42,678 --> 00:04:44,277
Yeon Seok and I filmed...

124
00:04:44,278 --> 00:04:45,848
- "The Royal Tailor" together.
- "The Royal Tailor."

125
00:04:46,018 --> 00:04:47,217
With Han Seok Kyu too.

126
00:04:47,218 --> 00:04:49,147
- You guys worked together.
- We filmed a movie together.

127
00:04:49,148 --> 00:04:51,217
- Right.
- It's been ten years.

128
00:04:51,218 --> 00:04:53,618
How many years...

129
00:04:54,058 --> 00:04:55,687
has your show been running so far?

130
00:04:55,688 --> 00:04:57,427
- About 3 years.
- This is our 3rd year.

131
00:04:57,428 --> 00:04:59,027
- Good job, Yeon Seok.
- We filmed 60-something episodes.

132
00:04:59,028 --> 00:05:00,527
- Good job, Yeon Seok.
- Okay.

133
00:05:00,528 --> 00:05:02,627
- I had a lot of fun.
- This isn't our final episode.

134
00:05:02,628 --> 00:05:03,628
I know.

135
00:05:05,568 --> 00:05:07,197
He made it sound like our show was ending.

136
00:05:07,198 --> 00:05:09,167
- No. I didn't mean that.
- You didn't, right?

137
00:05:09,168 --> 00:05:10,837
- It's only our opening segment.
- Right.

138
00:05:10,838 --> 00:05:12,607
(Chuckling)

139
00:05:12,608 --> 00:05:14,978
What should we get for lunch later?

140
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:17,077
Do you like pollack soup?

141
00:05:17,078 --> 00:05:18,078
I love it. Why?

142
00:05:18,079 --> 00:05:19,847
There's a great pollack soup place around here.

143
00:05:19,848 --> 00:05:21,017
- Really?
- Yes.

144
00:05:21,018 --> 00:05:22,188
Have you been going there since you were a kid?

145
00:05:22,688 --> 00:05:24,018
No, I've never eaten there.

146
00:05:24,288 --> 00:05:26,118
My mom told me their food was good.

147
00:05:26,558 --> 00:05:28,757
Seong Jae. Let's go there then.

148
00:05:28,758 --> 00:05:29,957
- Pollack soup sounds good, right?
- Pollack soup for lunch.

149
00:05:29,958 --> 00:05:31,188
I love pollack soup.

150
00:05:31,358 --> 00:05:33,398
- What about you, Soo?
- I love it.

151
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,297
But burgers sound good too.

152
00:05:35,298 --> 00:05:36,767
Burgers? That was random.

153
00:05:36,768 --> 00:05:37,968
(Burgers?)

154
00:05:38,598 --> 00:05:39,967
(Giving off an eccentric vibe)

155
00:05:39,968 --> 00:05:41,967
Burgers and pollack soup couldn't be more different.

156
00:05:41,968 --> 00:05:43,108
That's a big gap.

157
00:05:43,168 --> 00:05:45,478
Getting a burger after coming all the way here...

158
00:05:45,708 --> 00:05:48,577
No. I like both. Pollack soup and burgers sound good.

159
00:05:48,578 --> 00:05:51,007
- Let's see what happens later.
- Let's see then.

160
00:05:51,008 --> 00:05:54,378
Soo is so entertaining on a variety show.

161
00:05:56,148 --> 00:05:58,517
He has an unexpected side.

162
00:05:58,518 --> 00:06:00,187
- It's about time...
- Yes.

163
00:06:00,188 --> 00:06:02,227
- he showed his real character.
- Right.

164
00:06:02,228 --> 00:06:03,488
He's been in this industry long enough.

165
00:06:03,828 --> 00:06:06,097
- Of course.
- He's funny.

166
00:06:06,098 --> 00:06:09,098
He always says things that make me think a lot.

167
00:06:09,168 --> 00:06:10,897
What kind of thing does he say? Give us an example.

168
00:06:10,898 --> 00:06:13,538
Here's an example. When I asked him if he had eaten,

169
00:06:13,698 --> 00:06:16,908
he said, "Well, I..."

170
00:06:16,968 --> 00:06:20,038
He always takes long to answer.

171
00:06:20,138 --> 00:06:21,577
He could've just said "No, I didn't eat yet."

172
00:06:21,578 --> 00:06:23,207
- It would be over then.
- Right.

173
00:06:23,208 --> 00:06:27,217
I think you guys are so quick on your feet.

174
00:06:27,218 --> 00:06:29,747
I think that's just my pace.

175
00:06:29,748 --> 00:06:32,287
I do think about it, but it takes a while to answer it.

176
00:06:32,288 --> 00:06:34,458
- It takes some time for me.
- You need a moment to think.

177
00:06:34,688 --> 00:06:37,257
If today's games have a time limit...

178
00:06:37,258 --> 00:06:38,727
We have to be quick. You know?

179
00:06:38,728 --> 00:06:40,197
We have to finish the mission...

180
00:06:40,198 --> 00:06:41,657
- in 20 seconds.
- Really?

181
00:06:41,658 --> 00:06:44,428
We must be quick. We have a time limit.

182
00:06:44,728 --> 00:06:46,767
- That will be tough.
- Are you competitive?

183
00:06:46,768 --> 00:06:47,768
I'm competitive.

184
00:06:47,769 --> 00:06:49,467
You're competitive. But you don't enjoy games.

185
00:06:49,468 --> 00:06:50,567
Seong Jae is good at games.

186
00:06:50,568 --> 00:06:52,707
- But I'm not competitive.
- He is?

187
00:06:52,708 --> 00:06:55,377
- Seong Jae...
- So you have the skills.

188
00:06:55,378 --> 00:06:56,478
- But you're not competitive.
- I'm not.

189
00:06:56,978 --> 00:07:00,417
But the idea of this show is giving away the presents.

190
00:07:00,418 --> 00:07:02,587
- Right.
- I should work hard and do well.

191
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:04,187
- Let's work hard today.
- Yes.

192
00:07:04,188 --> 00:07:05,757
- Let's give them presents.
- Sounds good.

193
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:06,917
- Yes.
- Of course.

194
00:07:06,918 --> 00:07:08,558
Let's check where we're going today.

195
00:07:08,828 --> 00:07:10,828
- Her name is Park Ju Hee.
- Ju Hee.

196
00:07:11,388 --> 00:07:14,998
"In the jungle of cram schools for Korean, English, and math,"

197
00:07:15,258 --> 00:07:17,267
"I'm tending a small garden..."

198
00:07:17,268 --> 00:07:19,468
"where my students' imagination can bloom."

199
00:07:19,938 --> 00:07:22,667
Oh, my. "But I've been too busy taking care of my students."

200
00:07:22,668 --> 00:07:25,608
"So I've been just withering away."

201
00:07:26,138 --> 00:07:29,748
"Can you help me bloom again?"

202
00:07:31,078 --> 00:07:33,117
- Is she a teacher?
- She's tending a garden.

203
00:07:33,118 --> 00:07:34,717
I guess she's tending a garden...

204
00:07:34,718 --> 00:07:37,748
and running a place for kids.

205
00:07:37,788 --> 00:07:40,518
- But she's exhausted.
- Yes.

206
00:07:40,718 --> 00:07:42,188
- That's the point.
- She's withering away.

207
00:07:42,888 --> 00:07:45,557
She must be having a hard time looking after the kids.

208
00:07:45,558 --> 00:07:47,857
- Right. Shall we get going?
- Let's go.

209
00:07:47,858 --> 00:07:49,628
Shouldn't we finish this before we go?

210
00:07:50,068 --> 00:07:51,528
- Did you have breakfast?
- Wait.

211
00:07:52,868 --> 00:07:54,238
I thought you had breakfast.

212
00:07:54,268 --> 00:07:56,537
- Seong Jae, you should eat some.
- He's high-maintenance.

213
00:07:56,538 --> 00:07:58,507
- Okay.
- Let's finish this before we go.

214
00:07:58,508 --> 00:08:00,578
I haven't seen him after "You Quiz on the Block."

215
00:08:00,708 --> 00:08:02,578
- Well...
- Let's finish it.

216
00:08:02,978 --> 00:08:05,647
(After finishing their dessert...)

217
00:08:05,648 --> 00:08:07,178
Oh, it's so sunny.

218
00:08:07,548 --> 00:08:08,618
Today's weather is great.

219
00:08:09,018 --> 00:08:10,417
It's nice to see you guys...

220
00:08:10,418 --> 00:08:12,617
on this sunny day. It's been a while.

221
00:08:12,618 --> 00:08:13,718
Thanks for having us.

222
00:08:14,288 --> 00:08:16,287
He drove himself here today.

223
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:17,387
- Really?
- Yes.

224
00:08:17,388 --> 00:08:18,428
You drove your own car?

225
00:08:18,858 --> 00:08:20,858
- Of course.
- Your manager didn't come with you?

226
00:08:21,328 --> 00:08:22,797
It just happened that way today.

227
00:08:22,798 --> 00:08:24,128
- Really?
- Yes.

228
00:08:24,798 --> 00:08:26,467
We're just going to walk?

229
00:08:26,468 --> 00:08:28,867
- Well...
- How far is it?

230
00:08:28,868 --> 00:08:30,137
- Wait. This isn't the way.
- Okay.

231
00:08:30,138 --> 00:08:31,638
- We need to get on a bus.
- A bus?

232
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,908
- A bus? For how long?
- We need to get on a bus.

233
00:08:33,978 --> 00:08:35,407
Let's take Soo's car then.

234
00:08:35,408 --> 00:08:37,208
Yes, you drove here today.

235
00:08:38,178 --> 00:08:39,178
Shall we?

236
00:08:39,478 --> 00:08:40,678
- His car...
- Your car is here.

237
00:08:41,578 --> 00:08:43,918
If we're taking my car, I need to start it now.

238
00:08:45,148 --> 00:08:47,718
- That's cool.
- He really did it.

239
00:08:48,688 --> 00:08:51,088
(The cool guy is ready to give them a ride.)

240
00:08:51,188 --> 00:08:53,627
The bus stop is right here.

241
00:08:53,628 --> 00:08:55,158
- Let's take the bus.
- We'll take the bus.

242
00:08:55,698 --> 00:08:57,998
- Really? I should turn it off.
- Turn off the engine.

243
00:08:58,328 --> 00:08:59,367
(Turning off the engine)

244
00:08:59,368 --> 00:09:02,037
So we have to find the place just with the address?

245
00:09:02,038 --> 00:09:03,708
- We have to find it ourselves.
- I see.

246
00:09:04,268 --> 00:09:05,677
(Staring)

247
00:09:05,678 --> 00:09:07,477
That's the apartment I used to live in.

248
00:09:07,478 --> 00:09:09,378
Hey, the apartment looks nice.

249
00:09:10,308 --> 00:09:12,218
