- Right.

483
00:17:06,438 --> 00:17:08,797
Before this, I used to teach adults...

484
00:17:08,798 --> 00:17:10,807
- for a very long time.
- I see.

485
00:17:10,808 --> 00:17:12,507
- You used to teach adults?
- Yes.

486
00:17:12,508 --> 00:17:16,177
I used to teach only adults. But at some point,

487
00:17:16,178 --> 00:17:19,248
I wanted to change the paradigm of the modern art education.

488
00:17:19,448 --> 00:17:20,748
That was my goal.

489
00:17:21,118 --> 00:17:23,047
- She had a big goal.
- Yes.

490
00:17:23,048 --> 00:17:24,218
- She had a big goal.
- Right.

491
00:17:24,588 --> 00:17:26,957
- She had a big goal.
- Yes.

492
00:17:26,958 --> 00:17:29,017
I wanted to bring a new paradigm...

493
00:17:29,018 --> 00:17:32,557
to the modern art education. That's how I began.

494
00:17:32,558 --> 00:17:34,227
Isn't this what you mean?

495
00:17:34,228 --> 00:17:35,727
Many people say that you must be born with an artistic talent...

496
00:17:35,728 --> 00:17:37,267
- to pursue art.
- That's not true.

497
00:17:37,268 --> 00:17:39,637
- People should enjoy art.
- No. Right. We must have fun.

498
00:17:39,638 --> 00:17:41,137
That's the new paradigm you want, right?

499
00:17:41,138 --> 00:17:44,167
Of course. That's why I'm offering this kind of class.

500
00:17:44,168 --> 00:17:47,137
You said you wanted to bring a new paradigm, but your letter said...

501
00:17:47,138 --> 00:17:48,738
that you were withering away.

502
00:17:50,078 --> 00:17:51,407
- What's this discrepancy about?
- Right.

503
00:17:51,408 --> 00:17:53,117
- Right.
- Maybe, there's someone else.

504
00:17:53,118 --> 00:17:54,847
- Tell us about this discrepancy.
- Could there be another person?

505
00:17:54,848 --> 00:17:56,287
I bet there's someone else here.

506
00:17:56,288 --> 00:17:59,087
Hear me out. I love kids.

507
00:17:59,088 --> 00:18:01,187
- And I love my job.
- I see.

508
00:18:01,188 --> 00:18:02,757
Despite everything...

509
00:18:02,758 --> 00:18:04,787
As you know, kids have so much energy.

510
00:18:04,788 --> 00:18:05,957
- Absolutely.
- Yes.

511
00:18:05,958 --> 00:18:09,427
For example, I'd start my class in a good mood.

512
00:18:09,428 --> 00:18:10,867
- Right.
- But the kids listen to me...

513
00:18:10,868 --> 00:18:12,327
very briefly...

514
00:18:12,328 --> 00:18:14,397
when they talk nonstop.

515
00:18:14,398 --> 00:18:15,837
- You have to be a good listener.
- Right.

516
00:18:15,838 --> 00:18:19,167
While they work on their artwork, they must...

517
00:18:19,168 --> 00:18:21,177
- They want my attention and love.
- keep asking her questions. Right.

518
00:18:21,178 --> 00:18:22,877
Because they always demand my attention and love,

519
00:18:22,878 --> 00:18:26,647
my energy level which I worked hard to boost...

520
00:18:26,648 --> 00:18:30,148
- The energy level you boosted.
- goes down. I can feel the drop.

521
00:18:30,388 --> 00:18:32,547
- I see.
- So I always...

522
00:18:32,548 --> 00:18:34,987
encourage my students and show them my support.

523
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:36,227
- Compliments are important.
- Yes.

524
00:18:36,228 --> 00:18:39,357
I'd like some encouragement from someone too.

525
00:18:39,358 --> 00:18:40,358
- Right.
- I see.

526
00:18:40,359 --> 00:18:41,858
That's a fun part of this job.

527
00:18:42,328 --> 00:18:45,997
Are there any hobbies you enjoy doing in your free time?

528
00:18:45,998 --> 00:18:46,998
Do you have any hobbies?

529
00:18:46,999 --> 00:18:48,467
Actually,

530
00:18:48,468 --> 00:18:50,867
- I love dancing like you.
- You do?

531
00:18:50,868 --> 00:18:52,977
- When the BPM hits 130, - Really?

532
00:18:52,978 --> 00:18:54,837
- my heart burns with passion...
- I see.

533
00:18:54,838 --> 00:18:58,547
- and I can't stop moving my body.
- Right.

534
00:18:58,548 --> 00:19:00,577
So when I was in middle school,

535
00:19:00,578 --> 00:19:03,387
- H.O.T was very popular.
- Okay.

536
00:19:03,388 --> 00:19:05,117
My friends and I would divide up the roles.

537
00:19:05,118 --> 00:19:06,857
"You be Moon Hee Joon. I'll be Jang Woo Hyuk."

538
00:19:06,858 --> 00:19:09,357
We formed a group of our own.

539
00:19:09,358 --> 00:19:12,587
I guess people somehow heard that we were good dancers.

540
00:19:12,588 --> 00:19:15,227
There were 13 homerooms in my grade.

541
00:19:15,228 --> 00:19:18,768
Each homeroom invited us to dance for them.

542
00:19:18,868 --> 00:19:20,468
So we went during our breaks.

543
00:19:20,568 --> 00:19:22,797
We'd go to Homeroom One during a break.

544
00:19:22,798 --> 00:19:25,067
Then we'd go to Homeroom Three during the next break.

545
00:19:25,068 --> 00:19:26,167
So you guys held shows?

546
00:19:26,168 --> 00:19:28,177
- You went on a tour.
- Yes, we did.

547
00:19:28,178 --> 00:19:29,808
- You went to each homeroom.
- Right.

548
00:19:29,908 --> 00:19:31,708
Back then, I was on fire.

549
00:19:31,948 --> 00:19:35,148
- So I used to dance like crazy.
- I see.

550
00:19:35,448 --> 00:19:38,288
Which H.O.T's song do you want to dance to?

551
00:19:38,948 --> 00:19:40,017
What?

552
00:19:40,018 --> 00:19:42,888
(Ambushing her with a dance request)

553
00:19:43,088 --> 00:19:44,458
Didn't you want to dance?

554
00:19:44,658 --> 00:19:46,897
- It's been a while.
- Which song did you dance to?

555
00:19:46,898 --> 00:19:48,797
- What was it?
- It was "Descent of Warriors."

556
00:19:48,798 --> 00:19:50,268
- "Descent of Warriors."
- No.

557
00:19:50,368 --> 00:19:51,798
The choreography for that is pretty hard.

558
00:19:52,228 --> 00:19:54,937
- Hold on. "Descent of Warriors."
- It's been 30 years.

559
00:19:54,938 --> 00:19:56,638
- But you should still try.
- I forgot everything.

560
00:19:56,908 --> 00:19:58,467
- Oh, no.
- You need to relieve your stress.

561
00:19:58,468 --> 00:20:00,237
- Here's the thing.
- The intro is pretty intense.

562
00:20:00,238 --> 00:20:02,338
You said you were withering away.

563
00:20:02,978 --> 00:20:04,848
Well, I never say no. This is bad.

564
00:20:05,178 --> 00:20:07,277
- I forgot everything, though.
- Just try a little.

565
00:20:07,278 --> 00:20:08,377
Just the key moves.

566
00:20:08,378 --> 00:20:09,518
(Getting up)

567
00:20:09,548 --> 00:20:10,648
There she goes.

568
00:20:11,318 --> 00:20:12,418
Her walk is different.

569
00:20:14,058 --> 00:20:16,018
(Getting started)

570
00:20:16,428 --> 00:20:17,588
Gosh, she's...

571
00:20:18,328 --> 00:20:19,458
Oh, no.

572
00:20:20,898 --> 00:20:21,898
(Here comes the H.O.T from the old days.)

573
00:20:21,899 --> 00:20:22,967
Oh, my. That's good.

574
00:20:22,968 --> 00:20:24,198
(Here comes the H.O.T from the old days.)

575
00:20:24,428 --> 00:20:25,767
She still remembers it.

576
00:20:25,768 --> 00:20:29,738
(She's still got the moves even after all these years.)

577
00:20:34,038 --> 00:20:35,608
(The audience is very satisfied.)

578
00:20:36,008 --> 00:20:37,077
(In a trance)

579
00:20:37,078 --> 00:20:38,808
She's good. Gosh.

580
00:20:39,008 --> 00:20:40,947
- You're so good.
- Oh, no.

581
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:43,647
- My gosh.
- She totally deserved to perform.

582
00:20:43,648 --> 00:20:45,147
She totally deserved to go on that tour.

583
00:20:45,148 --> 00:20:47,258
It's been decades. But she still remembers the moves.

584
00:20:47,388 --> 00:20:48,717
- It's been 30 years.
- She's so talented.

585
00:20:48,718 --> 00:20:51,028
I think my friends will tease me for a century.

586
00:20:51,558 --> 00:20:53,257
You're a good dancer, by the way.

587
00:20:53,258 --> 00:20:54,597
- I'm pretty good, right?
- Yes.

588
00:20:54,598 --> 00:20:55,658
You were great.

589
00:20:55,758 --> 00:20:58,927
That brings me to this story. A while ago,

590
00:20:58,928 --> 00:21:00,867
I couldn't just live like this.

591
00:21:00,868 --> 00:21:02,767
- So I went to a dance school.
- Did you sign up?

592
00:21:02,768 --> 00:21:05,737
Yes. Many elementary and middle school students...

593
00:21:05,738 --> 00:21:07,238
- take dance classes these days.
- Right.

594
00:21:07,378 --> 00:21:10,508
The class I attended was full of elementary and middle school kids.

595
00:21:11,108 --> 00:21:12,448
I was the only adult.

596
00:21:12,648 --> 00:21:14,347
You saw elementary school kids even in that class.

597
00:21:14,348 --> 00:21:16,817
Since I give my all to everything,

598
00:21:16,818 --> 00:21:18,387
- I did my best.
- Of course.

599
00:21:18,388 --> 00:21:19,688
When I was dancing with them,

600
00:21:19,888 --> 00:21:23,728
I noticed that I was trying to outshine those kids.

601
00:21:24,728 --> 00:21:27,497
- It made me feel pathetic.
- You wanted to beat the kids?

602
00:21:27,498 --> 00:21:28,598
- Right.
- You wanted to beat them.

603
00:21:28,758 --> 00:21:30,227
- You got competitive.
- I got a reality check. Yes.

604
00:21:30,228 --> 00:21:32,498
Yes. I took the class very seriously.

605
00:21:33,038 --> 00:21:35,237
That's why I've been writing...

606
00:21:35,238 --> 00:21:36,707
and doing calligraphy quietly.

607
00:21:36,708 --> 00:21:38,908
You got to dance to "Descent of Warriors" after decades.

608
00:21:39,568 --> 00:21:40,907
You haven't thought about this for decades.

609
00:21:40,908 --> 00:21:42,277
When your friends see this,

610
00:21:42,278 --> 00:21:44,107
they'll call you up to dance to the song together.

611
00:21:44,108 --> 00:21:46,678
- Right. Are you watching? Call me.
- Yes.

612
00:21:47,178 --> 00:21:48,178
She was so good.

613
00:21:48,179 --> 00:21:50,417
We should encourage her and give her presents too.

614
00:21:50,418 --> 00:21:51,747
- Of course.
- We should make that work.

615
00:21:51,748 --> 00:21:54,658
All right. This is for you, Ju Hee.

616
00:21:54,918 --> 00:21:56,458
Oh, they're fortune cookies.

617
00:21:56,658 --> 00:21:58,887
Yes. It says what the present is.

618
00:21:58,888 --> 00:22:00,928
- Crack the cookie gently.
- Yes.

619
00:22:01,628 --> 00:22:02,697
Rounds 1, 2, and 3?

620
00:22:02,698 --> 00:22:05,668
Right. If we complete Round One, we can give her this present.

621
00:22:08,268 --> 00:22:10,138
"Keep both your artistic hands..."

622
00:22:10,908 --> 00:22:12,707
"and caregiving hands warm."

623
00:22:12,708 --> 00:22:14,178
"Burberry cashmere gloves."

624
00:22:14,908 --> 00:22:16,278
Burberry cashmere gloves.

625
00:22:17,008 --> 00:22:19,378
It's from a luxury brand. They're cashmere gloves.

626
00:22:19,578 --> 00:22:20,978
- Are they genuine?
- Burberry.

627
00:22:21,218 --> 00:22:22,378
- Of course.
- Hey.

628
00:22:22,778 --> 00:22:24,417
- How can we give a knockoff on TV?
- On TV...

629
00:22:24,418 --> 00:22:25,547
Oh, my.

630
00:22:25,548 --> 00:22:26,957
The presents are this fancy?

631
00:22:26,958 --> 00:22:28,018
They look warm.

632
00:22:28,118 --> 00:22:30,457
- What a cute pair.
- This is a cute pair of gloves.

633
00:22:30,458 --> 00:22:31,827
- She should wear them now.
- They'd look great on her.

634
00:22:31,828 --> 00:22:33,428
- What a cute pair for her outfit.
- What a cute pair.

635
00:22:33,658 --> 00:22:34,957
- Good luck!
- We got this.

636
00:22:34,958 --> 00:22:36,468
That's the present for Round One?

637
00:22:36,568 --> 00:22:37,927
(Palette Ping-Pong)

638
00:22:37,928 --> 00:22:39,597
(Bounce the ping-pong balls with a palette...)

639
00:22:39,598 --> 00:22:42,097
(and drop them in the water bucket.)

640
00:22:42,098 --> 00:22:44,508
(They must hold it like this.)

641
00:22:44,768 --> 00:22:46,637
We have to move around for this round.

642
00:22:46,638 --> 00:22:48,078
Where do we start? Here?

643
00:22:48,208 --> 00:22:50,078
- Start behind the desk.
- Behind the desk?

644
00:22:50,178 --> 00:22:52,748
All right. We can bounce the ball like this.

645
00:22:53,178 --> 00:22:55,047
- It's a relay race, right?
- It is.

646
00:22:55,048 --> 00:22:56,788
- We have to put in our thumb?
- Like this.

647
00:22:56,988 --> 00:22:58,047
Like this?

648
00:22:58,048 --> 00:22:59,217
- Can we use our right hand?
- We got this.

649
00:22:59,218 --> 00:23:00,817
- Good luck.
- We got this!

650
00:23:00,818 --> 00:23:02,388
We should be careful, so it doesn't hit our thumb.

651
00:23:03,628 --> 00:23:04,757
Hit it forward.

652
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:05,987
- We have to move forward.
- Wait.

653
00:23:05,988 --> 00:23:08,058
- We have to move forward?
- Right here...

654
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:09,457
My reach isn't as long...

655
00:23:09,458 --> 00:23:10,527
- as I thought.
- Wait.

656
00:23:10,528 --> 00:23:12,098
- Let's practice.
- Okay.

657
00:23:13,868 --> 00:23:14,968
- You have to hit it.
- Go for it.

658
00:23:16,708 --> 00:23:17,808
- You have to hit it.
- Go for it.

659
00:23:19,568 --> 00:23:20,577
What do I do?

660
00:23:20,578 --> 00:23:22,677
- Should we go in this order?
- That's the order?

661
00:23:22,678 --> 00:23:24,607
- Okay. The order doesn't matter.
- It should be random.

662
00:23:24,608 --> 00:23:26,308
It's okay as long as we all hit it once.

663
00:23:26,448 --> 00:23:27,877
- Let's call it out.
- Okay.

664
00:23:27,878 --> 00:23:29,517
Call it out when it looks a bit iffy.

665
00:23:29,518 --> 00:23:30,887
Go ahead. Pass it, Soo.

666
00:23:30,888 --> 00:23:32,048
- Okay.
- This is practice.

667
00:23:33,658 --> 00:23:35,458
- My gosh.
- Wait.

668
00:23:35,718 --> 00:23:37,488
(Taking turns to bomb the game)

669
00:23:37,788 --> 00:23:39,457
- You told him to pass it to you.
- I... Right.

670
00:23:39,458 --> 00:23:40,598
- Gosh.
- Here.

671
00:23:40,758 --> 00:23:44,067
I think it's better to pass it to Seong Jae.

672
00:23:44,068 --> 00:23:45,367
- Like this.
- I'll hit it if it's closer to me.

673
00:23:45,368 --> 00:23:46,497
- Okay.
- Okay.

674
00:23:46,498 --> 00:23:48,838
- We must move forward.
- Here's what I noticed.

675
00:23:49,198 --> 00:23:50,907
The ball shouldn't fall between two people.

676
00:23:50,908 --> 00:23:52,108
- Right.
- It's not going to work then.

677
00:23:52,308 --> 00:23:54,307
- The directions should be clear.
- Right.

678
00:23:54,308 --> 00:23:55,838
But your direction was off just now.

679
00:23:58,378 --> 00:23:59,408
My gosh.

680
00:23:59,778 --> 00:24:01,048
- Let's do this.
- Let's go.

681
00:24:01,448 --> 00:24:02,677
- Yeon Seok.
- It's practice.

682
00:24:02,678 --> 00:24:03,787
- Me? Okay.
- Here.

683
00:24:03,788 --> 00:24:05,218
- Yeon Seok. Here.
- Me? Okay.

684
00:24:07,558 --> 00:24:10,058
(Everyone hits the ball at least once.)

685
00:24:10,728 --> 00:24:11,758
Finish it.

686
00:24:12,288 --> 00:24:13,357
You can finish it.

687
00:24:13,358 --> 00:24:15,227
(The ball hits the bucket, and they fail.)

688
00:24:15,228 --> 00:24:16,898
- I'll pass it to you.
- Gosh.

689
00:24:17,368 --> 00:24:18,397
(Yeon Seok will finish it.)

690
00:24:18,398 --> 00:24:19,427
I should give a little more.

691
00:24:19,428 --> 00:24:20,497
Let's do this.

692
00:24:20,498 --> 00:24:22,438
(They're practicing again.)

693
00:24:23,708 --> 00:24:25,668
- Okay. Jae Seok.
- There you go.

694
00:24:25,908 --> 00:24:27,637
- Jae Seok. Just finish it.
- Yeon Seok.

695
00:24:27,638 --> 00:24:29,507
- Gosh, wait.
- Into the bucket.

696
00:24:29,508 --> 00:24:30,707
- Goal.
- There you go.

697
00:24:30,708 --> 00:24:31,847
- Goal.
- Into the bucket.

698
00:24:31,848 --> 00:24:32,907
- Goal.
- There you go.

699
00:24:32,908 --> 00:24:34,617
Hey, we got this. Okay.

700
00:24:34,618 --> 00:24:35,848
(Cheering)

701
00:24:35,948 --> 00:24:37,317
- Nice.
- Let's do this.

702
00:24:37,318 --> 00:24:39,048
- Let's do a group cheer.
- Let's go!

703
00:24:39,248 --> 00:24:41,358
- One, two, three. Let's go!
- One, two, three. Let's go!

704
00:24:43,018 --> 00:24:44,127
Let's go!

705
00:24:44,128 --> 00:24:45,327
In 1, 2, 3.

706
00:24:45,328 --> 00:24:47,727
- Here we go.
- Ready. Set...

707
00:24:47,728 --> 00:24:52,228
(Out of 10 total tries, they're on try number 1.)

708
00:24:57,568 --> 00:24:59,368
(The ball goes right between them.)

709
00:25:00,138 --> 00:25:01,577
- Why didn't they communicate?
- Soo!

710
00:25:01,578 --> 00:25:02,678
No.

711
00:25:03,778 --> 00:25:04,878
- Darn.
- No.

712
00:25:05,278 --> 00:25:06,378
Come on.

713
00:25:06,478 --> 00:25:08,078
- What...
- Soo.

714
00:25:08,248 --> 00:25:09,478
You said you were going to call it.

715
00:25:11,118 --> 00:25:12,787
- I'm sorry.
- Yeon Seok...

716
00:25:12,788 --> 00:25:13,918
- Soo.
- Okay.

717
00:25:14,288 --> 00:25:16,258
I got startled. I'm sorry.

718
00:25:16,588 --> 00:25:17,657
You should start.

719
00:25:17,658 --> 00:25:19,328
- You should start.
- Okay.

720
00:25:19,688 --> 00:25:21,097
- Let's try again.
- Soo.

721
00:25:21,098 --> 00:25:22,127
This is your second try.

722
00:25:22,128 --> 00:25:23,597
- We wasted our first try.
- Okay.

723
00:25:23,598 --> 00:25:24,697
Let's do this. Come on.

724
00:25:24,698 --> 00:25:26,468
- Let's do this.
- Stay sharp.

725
00:25:26,698 --> 00:25:28,167
- We got this.
- Ready.

726
00:25:28,168 --> 00:25:29,467
- Should we go for it?
- Here we go.

727
00:25:29,468 --> 00:25:31,267
In 1, 2, 3.

728
00:25:31,268 --> 00:25:33,607
- Here we go.
- Ready. Set...

729
00:25:33,608 --> 00:25:38,408
(Out of 10 total tries, they're on try number 2.)

730
00:25:38,808 --> 00:25:39,878
Here.

731
00:25:44,318 --> 00:25:45,848
- I'll finish it. No!
- Okay.

732
00:25:46,718 --> 00:25:47,758
- It hit my thumb.
- It's okay.

733
00:25:48,018 --> 00:25:50,127
We have to be careful not to hit our thumb.

734
00:25:50,128 --> 00:25:51,288
- I'll finish it.
- Okay.

735
00:25:51,488 --> 00:25:52,558
No!

736
00:25:53,828 --> 00:25:54,928
It's okay.

737
00:25:55,058 --> 00:25:57,168
We have to be careful not to hit our thumb.

738
00:25:57,728 --> 00:25:58,997
(He didn't expect his thumb to get in the way.)

739
00:25:58,998 --> 00:26:00,668
- Gosh, when we practiced...
- This is...

740
00:26:01,538 --> 00:26:03,307
- All right. Calm down.
- Wait.

741
00:26:03,308 --> 00:26:04,837
- That shouldn't have happened.
- Calm down.

742
00:26:04,838 --> 00:26:07,477
- It shouldn't be this hard.
- Stay calm.

743
00:26:07,478 --> 00:26:08,478
Stay calm.

744
00:26:08,479 --> 00:26:09,677
(She's starting to get anxious.)

745
00:26:09,678 --> 00:26:11,848
Actually, Round One is doable.

746
00:26:12,008 --> 00:26:15,148
- Our teamwork is off.
- All right. Let's do a group cheer.

747
00:26:15,248 --> 00:26:16,617
- Okay. Ju Hee.
- We got this.

748
