There's no space left for me at all.

1509
00:53:31,520 --> 00:53:32,529
(A fierce battle for the best spot)

1510
00:53:32,530 --> 00:53:34,830
- Come on.
- Hold on. I can't...

1511
00:53:35,430 --> 00:53:36,430
Come on.

1512
00:53:36,730 --> 00:53:38,000
Then I'll...

1513
00:53:39,100 --> 00:53:40,569
- grab it from here.
- Hey.

1514
00:53:40,570 --> 00:53:41,640
Hey.

1515
00:53:42,470 --> 00:53:44,199
- Here.
- Hey.

1516
00:53:44,200 --> 00:53:46,140
That was a wrong decision!

1517
00:53:46,710 --> 00:53:48,439
(Laughing)

1518
00:53:48,440 --> 00:53:50,080
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three!

1519
00:53:50,740 --> 00:53:51,749
Hey!

1520
00:53:51,750 --> 00:53:52,780
- Two, three!
- Two, three!

1521
00:53:53,250 --> 00:53:54,310
Hey!

1522
00:53:58,590 --> 00:53:59,619
Hey!

1523
00:53:59,620 --> 00:54:01,349
(He gets a large piece at the very end.)

1524
00:54:01,350 --> 00:54:03,420
(A tiny piece)

1525
00:54:03,520 --> 00:54:05,029
(Soo will pay the bills.)

1526
00:54:05,030 --> 00:54:07,389
Thank you, Soo.

1527
00:54:07,390 --> 00:54:09,029
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Soo.

1528
00:54:09,030 --> 00:54:11,330
- Thank you.
- How could it end like this?

1529
00:54:12,230 --> 00:54:13,970
- Goodness.
- Goodness. That tastes good.

1530
00:54:14,170 --> 00:54:16,969
The person holding the middle is at a disadvantage.

1531
00:54:16,970 --> 00:54:18,369
- Thank you, Soo.
- I was going to...

1532
00:54:18,370 --> 00:54:19,710
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1533
00:54:20,740 --> 00:54:22,180
While you're at it,

1534
00:54:22,840 --> 00:54:24,309
- could I also get the nurungji...
- Sure.

1535
00:54:24,310 --> 00:54:25,450
This one as well.

1536
00:54:25,650 --> 00:54:26,780
Two of these.

1537
00:54:27,150 --> 00:54:29,050
- You'll need to get at least 4.
- We'll get 2.

1538
00:54:29,180 --> 00:54:30,220
Okay.

1539
00:54:31,020 --> 00:54:32,149
- It works.
- Please sign.

1540
00:54:32,150 --> 00:54:33,719
(It's Go Soo's treat.)

1541
00:54:33,720 --> 00:54:35,659
- We'll come back again.
- Thank you!

1542
00:54:35,660 --> 00:54:36,689
Thank you.

1543
00:54:36,690 --> 00:54:37,790
Thank you for the meal, Soo.

1544
00:54:38,490 --> 00:54:40,660
- The meal...
- I'm really happy, Soo.

1545
00:54:40,830 --> 00:54:43,099
I feel more comfortable when I pay for the meal.

1546
00:54:43,100 --> 00:54:44,160
Let's go now.

1547
00:54:46,370 --> 00:54:47,430
It's this one.

1548
00:54:48,070 --> 00:54:49,300
The taxi?

1549
00:54:49,970 --> 00:54:51,970
- Have some rice puffs.
- Thank you.

1550
00:54:52,510 --> 00:54:55,040
- It's too nice to eat.
- Have one more.

1551
00:54:56,110 --> 00:54:57,579
Have some rice puffs.

1552
00:54:57,580 --> 00:54:58,679
Thank you.

1553
00:54:58,680 --> 00:54:59,680
(They share the rice puffs.)

1554
00:54:59,681 --> 00:55:00,780
We should put on the seatbelts.

1555
00:55:01,980 --> 00:55:03,320
After having the pollack soup,

1556
00:55:03,880 --> 00:55:06,619
the guilt from before seems to go away.

1557
00:55:06,620 --> 00:55:08,050
- I forgot about that.
- Yes.

1558
00:55:08,290 --> 00:55:10,390
- I feel recharged.
- Yes.

1559
00:55:10,690 --> 00:55:13,189
We should definitely succeed in the next one.

1560
00:55:13,190 --> 00:55:15,459
- This...
- I'll feel so bad if we fail.

1561
00:55:15,460 --> 00:55:16,730
I don't think I'll be able to sleep tonight.

1562
00:55:17,060 --> 00:55:18,160
Yes.

1563
00:55:18,300 --> 00:55:19,570
Please give me one more, Yeon Shik.

1564
00:55:21,070 --> 00:55:22,340
You just can't stop eating this.

1565
00:55:22,840 --> 00:55:25,070
- You can't stop.
- I'm crazy about it.

1566
00:55:25,570 --> 00:55:26,570
(Crunchy)

1567
00:55:26,910 --> 00:55:28,640
- Seong Jae?
- I'll have one more.

1568
00:55:31,380 --> 00:55:33,050
I tell myself I'll just have 1 or 2, but...

1569
00:55:34,880 --> 00:55:36,950
The restaurant your mother...

1570
00:55:37,450 --> 00:55:38,949
- recommended was really...
- It was good.

1571
00:55:38,950 --> 00:55:40,049
- Seriously.
- Thank you.

1572
00:55:40,050 --> 00:55:41,289
Thank her for us.

1573
00:55:41,290 --> 00:55:43,490
- I'll tell her.
- Thank you, Mother.

1574
00:55:43,890 --> 00:55:45,560
(Smiling)

1575
00:55:46,530 --> 00:55:47,630
I should stop eating.

1576
00:55:49,700 --> 00:55:51,160
I'll have just one more.

1577
00:55:52,870 --> 00:55:53,930
Jae Seok?

1578
00:55:56,700 --> 00:55:57,770
Could you give me one more?

1579
00:56:00,170 --> 00:56:01,370
This is really the last one.

1580
00:56:02,680 --> 00:56:04,140
- For real.
- This is really the last one.

1581
00:56:04,910 --> 00:56:07,780
- It freshens up your mouth.
- Right.

1582
00:56:09,220 --> 00:56:10,720
- It cleanses the palate.
- Yes.

1583
00:56:11,790 --> 00:56:12,890
Give me one more.

1584
00:56:12,990 --> 00:56:14,790
(Laughing)

1585
00:56:15,790 --> 00:56:16,820
Yes.

1586
00:56:16,960 --> 00:56:18,490
He's fallen for the rice puffs.

1587
00:56:19,760 --> 00:56:21,690
The place we're going to...

1588
00:56:22,700 --> 00:56:24,330
is some kind of court.

1589
00:56:24,660 --> 00:56:25,730
A court?

1590
00:56:26,070 --> 00:56:27,670
Yang Jong Cheol.

1591
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:30,399
"He leaves for work before sunrise and comes home after dark."

1592
00:56:30,400 --> 00:56:31,400
What?

1593
00:56:31,401 --> 00:56:33,069
"My dad has been working hard for his family..."

1594
00:56:33,070 --> 00:56:34,709
"for more than 30 years."

1595
00:56:34,710 --> 00:56:36,980
- "I want to give him a surprise."
- To the father.

1596
00:56:37,380 --> 00:56:39,909
"Please give my dad an unforgettable break..."

1597
00:56:39,910 --> 00:56:42,079
"on the court..."

1598
00:56:42,080 --> 00:56:44,450
"where he's played a lifetime of nonstop rallies."

1599
00:56:45,120 --> 00:56:46,820
- The court?
- Dad's court?

1600
00:56:47,320 --> 00:56:48,389
Basketball?

1601
00:56:48,390 --> 00:56:49,790
- Basketball court?
- Tennis court?

1602
00:56:50,660 --> 00:56:52,329
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1603
00:56:52,330 --> 00:56:53,460
I hope you succeed.

1604
00:56:53,890 --> 00:56:55,459
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1605
00:56:55,460 --> 00:56:57,330
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you.

1606
00:56:57,500 --> 00:56:58,600
Let's succeed for real.

1607
00:56:59,100 --> 00:57:00,270
I want to succeed.

1608
00:57:00,870 --> 00:57:01,970
We should succeed.

1609
00:57:02,340 --> 00:57:03,600
Okay.

1610
00:57:04,370 --> 00:57:05,540
We're here.

1611
00:57:06,070 --> 00:57:07,810
It's a tennis court.

1612
00:57:07,940 --> 00:57:10,680
So he plays tennis.

1613
00:57:10,780 --> 00:57:12,749
- Hello.
- Hello.

1614
00:57:12,750 --> 00:57:14,879
- Who's Yang Jong Cheol?
- They're all here.

1615
00:57:14,880 --> 00:57:16,079
Right. Goodness.

1616
00:57:16,080 --> 00:57:17,250
- Hello.
- His daughters...

1617
00:57:17,350 --> 00:57:19,649
So the daughters sent the letter.

1618
00:57:19,650 --> 00:57:20,889
- Yes.
- That's right.

1619
00:57:20,890 --> 00:57:22,319
- Hello.
- Hello.

1620
00:57:22,320 --> 00:57:23,420
Goodness.

1621
00:57:23,820 --> 00:57:25,359
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

1622
00:57:25,360 --> 00:57:27,789
- Hello.
- I know it's obvious,

1623
00:57:27,790 --> 00:57:30,099
but you really look like your father.

1624
00:57:30,100 --> 00:57:32,029
(The three daughters share their father's kind look.)

1625
00:57:32,030 --> 00:57:35,469
Do you work...

1626
00:57:35,470 --> 00:57:37,200
- as a coach here?
- Yes.

1627
00:57:37,440 --> 00:57:40,370
I currently work as a tennis instructor...

1628
00:57:40,570 --> 00:57:42,610
in Suji-gu, Yongin.

1629
00:57:42,940 --> 00:57:44,109
It's been 38 years.

1630
00:57:44,110 --> 00:57:45,780
Thirty-eight years?

1631
00:57:47,250 --> 00:57:50,180
- Your face has gotten pretty tan.
- That's right.

1632
00:57:50,380 --> 00:57:52,989
Excluding the area covered by the sunglasses.

1633
00:57:52,990 --> 00:57:55,189
Even when it's cold...

1634
00:57:55,190 --> 00:57:58,530
My daughters always called me a panda.

1635
00:57:59,560 --> 00:58:00,659
This part is lighter.

1636
00:58:00,660 --> 00:58:01,689
(A reverse panda)

1637
00:58:01,690 --> 00:58:03,499
Even his ankles look like he's wearing socks.

1638
00:58:03,500 --> 00:58:05,229
- This part is lighter.
- Right.

1639
00:58:05,230 --> 00:58:06,399
But the skin above is really dark.

1640
00:58:06,400 --> 00:58:09,140
- Since he plays tennis in shorts.
- That's right.

1641
00:58:09,370 --> 00:58:11,440
Were you all born and raised...

1642
00:58:11,600 --> 00:58:12,669
- in this area?
- Yes.

1643
00:58:12,670 --> 00:58:13,670
- That's right.
- Oh, really?

1644
00:58:13,671 --> 00:58:15,339
- Seong Jae is also...
- We know.

1645
00:58:15,340 --> 00:58:16,579
He's really famous around here.

1646
00:58:16,580 --> 00:58:17,940
Since he's from here...

1647
00:58:18,380 --> 00:58:20,110
(Laughing proudly)

1648
00:58:20,910 --> 00:58:22,720
- He's...
- The son of Suji.

1649
00:58:23,120 --> 00:58:25,589
Everyone in Suji knows. He's the son of Suji.

1650
00:58:25,590 --> 00:58:28,089
Seong Jae suddenly sat arrogantly.

1651
00:58:28,090 --> 00:58:29,290
(The star born in Suji is already famous here.)

1652
00:58:29,960 --> 00:58:31,560
We went to the same academy.

1653
00:58:31,720 --> 00:58:32,829
- Which one was it?
- The academy.

1654
00:58:32,830 --> 00:58:34,359
Did you go to Daesung Academy?

1655
00:58:34,360 --> 00:58:35,630
- In Wonhee Castle?
- Yes.

1656
00:58:35,900 --> 00:58:38,299
I told you about Wonhee Castle earlier.

1657
00:58:38,300 --> 00:58:39,699
- Oh, really?
- The academy.

1658
00:58:39,700 --> 00:58:42,039
- The one in Wonhee Castle?
- We were there.

1659
00:58:42,040 --> 00:58:44,570
- Wonhee Castle.
- I met a classmate.

1660
00:58:44,670 --> 00:58:47,309
- It's so fascinating.
- I told you you'd meet them.

1661
00:58:47,310 --> 00:58:48,809
- Wonhee Castle.
- It's in front of our house.

1662
00:58:48,810 --> 00:58:50,909
I was in Seongbok-dong earlier...

1663
00:58:50,910 --> 00:58:52,810
and got out of the car as it was Suji.

1664
00:58:53,510 --> 00:58:54,709
I didn't recognize the place.

1665
00:58:54,710 --> 00:58:56,080
- It has changed so much.
- So much has changed.

1666
00:58:56,420 --> 00:58:58,049
- I lived in Sanghyeon-dong...
- We know.

1667
00:58:58,050 --> 00:58:59,689
- for about 15 or 16 years.
- Right.

1668
00:58:59,690 --> 00:59:01,149
Do you live in Sanghyeon-dong now?

1669
00:59:01,150 --> 00:59:02,159
I live in Seongbok-dong now.

1670
00:59:02,160 --> 00:59:03,589
- Our parents' place is in Seongbok.
- We live in Seongbok-dong.

1671
00:59:03,590 --> 00:59:04,620
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

1672
00:59:05,190 --> 00:59:08,530
We all live in the same country, so...

1673
00:59:08,600 --> 00:59:10,229
- I'm so sorry.
- You've been talking too long...

1674
00:59:10,230 --> 00:59:11,900
about your town.

1675
00:59:12,100 --> 00:59:13,970
We felt a bit left out.

1676
00:59:14,200 --> 00:59:15,540
I was just so glad to see them.

1677
00:59:18,440 --> 00:59:20,940
So, the three daughters applied for our show?

1678
00:59:21,070 --> 00:59:22,779
I applied for it.

1679
00:59:22,780 --> 00:59:24,110
I see.

1680
00:59:24,280 --> 00:59:28,110
On my wedding day, my dad and my father-in-law...

1681
00:59:28,310 --> 00:59:31,020
performed a wedding song while playing the guitar.

1682
00:59:31,180 --> 00:59:33,590
It became such a good memory.

1683
00:59:33,690 --> 00:59:36,789
So, I also wanted to make a fun memory for him...

1684
00:59:36,790 --> 00:59:40,629
as he has a monotonous daily routine. That's why I applied.

1685
00:59:40,630 --> 00:59:42,260
(Smiling widely)

1686
00:59:43,030 --> 00:59:46,399
You practiced playing the guitar with your in-law?

1687
00:59:46,400 --> 00:59:48,299
Yes. I don't play the guitar well,

1688
00:59:48,300 --> 00:59:50,440
and my in-law is from Jinju.

1689
00:59:50,540 --> 00:59:51,669
(He's from Jinju.)

1690
00:59:51,670 --> 00:59:54,369
He's from Jinju, and he's known as a semi-professional singer.

1691
00:59:54,370 --> 00:59:55,979
- Oh, really?
- Oh, is he that good?

1692
00:59:55,980 --> 00:59:56,980
Yes.

1693
00:59:56,981 --> 00:59:59,679
- He gave me a score.
- Okay.

1694
00:59:59,680 --> 01:00:02,480
- It was a song I'd never heard of.
- Right.

1695
01:00:02,720 --> 01:00:04,850
I learned to play it by myself for about a year.

1696
01:00:05,390 --> 01:00:07,549
- Gosh.
- You prepared for it for a year?

1697
01:00:07,550 --> 01:00:08,890
- Yes.
- Goodness.

1698
01:00:09,420 --> 01:00:12,160
Our team name was Hwan and Cheol.

1699
01:00:12,530 --> 01:00:13,759
We combined our names' last syllables.

1700
01:00:13,760 --> 01:00:14,790
(A year-long project, Hwan and Cheol)

1701
01:00:15,190 --> 01:00:17,330
(He loves this story.)

1702
01:00:17,960 --> 01:00:20,699
(The wedding day of his precious daughter)

1703
01:00:20,700 --> 01:00:24,340
(Hwan, Cheol)

1704
01:00:25,000 --> 01:00:30,840
(The most special gift from a father)

1705
01:00:31,610 --> 01:00:34,609
- That must've been fun.
- This is really...

1706
01:00:34,610 --> 01:00:38,450
A father and a daughter may get along when they're young,

1707
01:00:38,720 --> 01:00:41,119
- but as they grow up, - That's right.

1708
01:00:41,120 --> 01:00:43,990
- They get awkward.
- they could get awkward.

1709
01:00:44,260 --> 01:00:46,289
But you're all still very close.

1710
01:00:46,290 --> 01:00:48,030
When I think of my dad,

1711
01:00:48,430 --> 01:00:52,130
I always say he's someone I admire and respect the most.

1712
01:00:53,630 --> 01:00:56,199
You know the questions they ask when you forget your password?

1713
01:00:56,200 --> 01:00:57,339
When you sign up for a website,

1714
01:00:57,340 --> 01:00:58,869
the hint question is, "Who do you respect the most?"

1715
01:00:58,870 --> 01:01:00,009
- Such questions pop up.
- A hint question.

1716
01:01:00,010 --> 01:01:02,679
Yes. I always type in my dad's name.

1717
01:01:02,680 --> 01:01:04,710
I never forget the answer because it's always the same.

1718
01:01:04,810 --> 01:01:07,280
(Na Eun's father is moved.)

1719
01:01:07,380 --> 01:01:09,880
(The father of three is moved too.)

1720
01:01:10,250 --> 01:01:12,990
That's how much I respect him.

1721
01:01:13,220 --> 01:01:15,020
(Laughing brightly)

1722
01:01:15,320 --> 01:01:16,920
Father seems so happy.

1723
01:01:17,560 --> 01:01:19,660
(He can't hide how proud he feels.)

1724
01:01:19,730 --> 01:01:21,459
- He's really sweet too.
- Right.

1725
01:01:21,460 --> 01:01:22,859
He's like our friend.

1726
01:01:22,860 --> 01:01:24,399
He also takes the bait every time.

1727
01:01:24,400 --> 01:01:25,500
Takes the bait every time?

1728
01:01:25,870 --> 01:01:27,600
How can you say that to your father?

1729
01:01:28,470 --> 01:01:30,369
(A father who takes the bait every time)

1730
01:01:30,370 --> 01:01:33,069
- You mean it's fun to tease him.
- Yes. That's right.

1731
01:01:33,070 --> 01:01:35,709
His surprised expression is really cute.

1732
01:01:35,710 --> 01:01:36,879
- Oh, really?
- So, on his way home from work,

1733
01:01:36,880 --> 01:01:38,039
one would hide in the parking lot,

1734
01:01:38,040 --> 01:01:40,510
one would hide at the front door, one would hide in front of the room.

1735
01:01:40,610 --> 01:01:42,750
We startle him three times in a row when he gets home.

1736
01:01:43,080 --> 01:01:44,450
We kept videos of those moments.

1737
01:01:44,850 --> 01:01:45,990
Yang Jong Cheol.

1738
01:01:46,590 --> 01:01:47,789
You scared me!

1739
01:01:47,790 --> 01:01:49,559
(A reaction that's fun to tease)

1740
01:01:49,560 --> 01:01:50,790
I got goosebumps.

1741
01:01:51,360 --> 01:01:53,590
Why do you girls tease your dad so much?

1742
01:01:54,430 --> 01:01:56,859
- It's fun.
- He's easy to take the bait.

1743
01:01:56,860 --> 01:01:58,560
Even if he's not easy to take the bait...

1744
01:01:59,330 --> 01:02:00,870
It scares him so much.

1745
01:02:01,100 --> 01:02:03,169
Your daughters said...

1746
01:02:03,170 --> 01:02:05,970
you're the kind of father who takes the bait easily.

1747
01:02:06,270 --> 01:02:08,609
What do you think of your daughters?

1748
01:02:08,610 --> 01:02:11,180
- Yes. Let's start with the eldest.
- Yes. One by one.

1749
01:02:12,040 --> 01:02:14,410
First of all, she's really thoughtful.

1750
01:02:14,710 --> 01:02:16,279
Maybe because she's the eldest,

1751
01:02:16,280 --> 01:02:19,550
she always thinks of me and is considerate.

1752
01:02:19,920 --> 01:02:21,520
Our second daughter...

1753
01:02:21,650 --> 01:02:23,760
is in a way...

1754
01:02:24,220 --> 01:02:26,259
What? You have nothing to say?

1755
01:02:26,260 --> 01:02:27,659
(He can't continue.)

1756
01:02:27,660 --> 01:02:29,360
- This makes her...
- What is it?

1757
01:02:30,130 --> 01:02:31,530
- You have nothing to say?
- Her temper...

1758
01:02:31,600 --> 01:02:32,770
- Temper?
- Temper?

1759
01:02:33,170 --> 01:02:34,969
- Dad, you can't say that.
- She has a bit of a temper?

1760
01:02:34,970 --> 01:02:37,399
